From the 023 console run: the two compute programs still failing (b38668a2c75d97ff and
0ba3144c5df5d1f9, "Invalid U16 selector 1", about 35 skipped dispatches a second) came from the
I2F lowering. Ampere's selector counts half-words for a 16-bit source, Maxwell's counts bytes, so
the high half was written as byte 1. It is now byte 2. Bumps the translator salt.
Handle programs also take a word of a vector merged from branches (703 of the 023 run's 1024
handle-zero cases: CompositeExtractU32x4 of a Phi of 128-bit loads), keeping the defined incoming
value as the Phi rule does.

